text:
The chat should show visuals the agent asks for, drawn with the design system's new flow and map components (see the design system's NOTES.md and the architecture's new decision on visuals in the chat). Design how they look in the transcript:

a flow in the agent's message, and a map with the parts a change touched;
several visuals in one message, mixed with text;
a block Prelude couldn't read (unknown part id, wrong format): shown as the agent wrote it, with a quiet note saying why;
narrow chat column and pop-out window;
while the agent is still writing the block (streaming).
Add transcript states for each, and rules for what's checked and what happens when it fails. Each part on a visual links to its page in the architecture.

These transcript views are also the ask and fix conversation's (server/views/_session.eta); cover its width too.

